<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: SAS — Learning the Order of Thought in Diffusion LMs</h2>
    <p>Masked diffusion language models decode by iteratively revealing tokens from a masked sequence, and the order in which they unmask tokens is a hidden degree of freedom that has been largely ignored. Self-Aware Scheduling, or SAS, trains a lightweight order policy to maximize the frozen diffusion model's own pathwise log-likelihood — a dense, self-referential reward that assigns credit to every individual reveal decision.</p>
    <p>On Sudoku with a 1B masked diffusion model, SAS improves puzzle accuracy from 82% under the best heuristic schedule to 91.8%, and reaches 97.5% with optional second-stage fine-tuning. On GSM8K math reasoning with LLaDA-8B, pass at 1 improves from 64% to 76%. Remarkably, the human expert ordering scores only 76.6% — well below the naïve confidence schedule — because the optimal order for a pretrained diffusion model is shaped by the model's own uncertainty landscape, not human logical intuition.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：SAS——扩散语言模型中的思维顺序学习</h2>
    <p>掩码扩散语言模型通过逐步揭示被掩码序列中的标记来完成解码，而标记的揭示顺序是一个长期被忽视的隐藏自由度。自感知调度（SAS）训练一个轻量级顺序策略，以最大化冻结扩散模型自身的路径对数似然——这是一个密集的自参照奖励，能够为每个单独的揭示决策分配信用。</p>
    <p>在使用1B参数掩码扩散模型的数独任务上，SAS将谜题准确率从最佳启发式调度的82%提升至91.8%，配合可选的第二阶段微调可达97.5%。在LLaDA-8B的GSM8K数学推理任务上，pass@1从64%提升至76%。值得注意的是，人类专家顺序仅得76.6%，远低于朴素置信度调度——因为预训练扩散模型的最优顺序由模型自身的不确定性格局决定，而非人类的逻辑直觉。</p>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

